  "summary": "Install-time beacon exfiltrates host metadata to hardcoded bare-IP endpoint",
  "details": "The package is a non-functional shim whose index.js exports a Proxy of no-op functions, with no real functionality. Its only effect is a beacon script (beacon.cjs) wired to both the postinstall lifecycle hook and the main module, which POSTs the installer's hostname, install path, current working directory, and Node version to the hardcoded bare-IP endpoint http://185.158.107.175:8787/_ah/dc over plain HTTP. The destination is unauthenticated, is not the package's publisher, and fires automatically on npm install and on any require() of the package. The payload composition and delivery shape are consistent with a dependency-confusion / name-squat beacon.",
